TITLE: Measure the interpreter at corpus scale once it exists
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Nothing in the engine assessment was measured at real corpus scale except
pySHACL, which validated the 489-file corpus in 43 ms. Once the
standard-library interpreter exists, measure a per-write fire() in the daemon,
a whole-corpus contract check, and a whole-corpus ripple from one MECHANISM
edit, over the real corpus, and record the numbers on this node. Each is of
order nodes times invariants times edges; a number over the scribe check's 2.1
s budget is a finding.
<<<
